edDate":"2026-09-20","seoDescription":"Ranked list of enterprise AI SDRs. Artisan, Regie.ai, Agentforce, Apollo, Clay, and 11x compared on autonomy, CRM depth, governance, and cost.","readTime":"6 minutes","tag":"AI SDR","keyTakeAways":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"ckzcYHBJgdJYUbNtBZpZX","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-09-20T02:01:41.226Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-20T02:01:41.226Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"blogKeyTakeaways"}},"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"keyTakeAways":[{"keyTakeAways":"Artisan's Ava is an autonomous AI BDR that finds leads, writes personalized multi-channel outreach, handles replies, and books qualified meetings, and teams running an autonomous AI BDR typically generate pipeline at around one-fifth the cost of a human BDR."},{"keyTakeAways":"Enterprise-grade means autonomy you can actually govern: campaign-level review modes, plain-language escalation rules, and a full audit trail."},{"keyTakeAways":"A US BDR costs $60K+ base ($120K-200K fully loaded) with 3-6 months of ramp and roughly 14 months of average tenure. An AI SDR compresses that math."},{"keyTakeAways":"SumUp generates leads at $52 cost per lead with Ava, and SaaStr sent 6,892 emails at a 3.6% positive response rate in about six weeks."},{"keyTakeAways":"Salesforce found 81% of sales teams are experimenting with or have fully implemented AI, and Gartner found B2B sellers who effectively partner with AI tools are 3.7x more likely to meet quota."},{"keyTakeAways":"Typical enterprise outbound stacks run 5-8 point tools at $100K+/year before headcount. The leading AI SDRs consolidate that spend."}],"blogName":"What is the best AI SDR for enterprise sales teams?"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/4fCBzvKJoCmI6sNaWLGthe/ee84344f587b1b89155b60e568adc5a6/best-ai-sdr-enterprise-cover.webp","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"Best AI SDR for enterprise sales teams in 2026"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan is the best AI SDR for enterprise sales teams in 2026. Its AI BDR, ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/ai-sales-agent"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"Ava","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":", owns the entire outbound workflow, from sourcing leads to handling replies and booking meetings, drawing on a database of over 250 million B2B professionals across over 200 countries, plus Artisan Local Data with over 250 million local businesses, with the controls enterprises require: escalation rules, review modes, audit trails, and native Salesforce and HubSpot sync. Regie.ai and Salesforce Agentforce SDR are credible alternatives, and the right choice depends on your CRM standardization and how much autonomy you want.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What \"enterprise-grade\" actually means for an AI SDR","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Most AI SDR comparisons rank tools on email volume and price. Enterprise buyers fail or succeed on five harder dimensions.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Autonomy with control.","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" Autonomy should be a dial, not a switch. You want full autopilot or review-and-approve per campaign, plain-language escalation rules (\"if the lead mentions pricing, escalate\"), configurable autonomous replies, and an audit trail of every action the AI took.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"CRM depth.","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" Native Salesforce and HubSpot sync is table stakes. The real tests are dynamic CRM lists as campaign sources, owner mapping so outreach goes out on behalf of each account owner, and CRM-driven do-not-contact logic that auto-excludes accounts with active deals.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Deliverability infrastructure at scale.","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" Sending tens of thousands of emails monthly without burning your domain requires managed secondary mailboxes with automated sending ramp-up, inbox placement testing, dynamic send limits, and bounce-pattern detection that auto-pauses unhealthy mailboxes. See how Artisan handles this in its ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/features/email-deliverability"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"email deliverability infrastructure","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":".","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Security posture.","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" SOC 2, GDPR-compliant data handling, penetration testing, SSO, and role-based permissions. If a vendor can't survive your security review, nothing else matters.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Dedicated support.","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" Enterprise outbound is as much a strategy problem as a software problem. Look for a forward-deployed strategist and a dedicated CSM rather than a ticket queue.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The best AI SDRs for enterprise sales teams in 2026, ranked","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"1. Artisan (Ava)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{"target":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"5ptpf9UDcr17VTzMiDLsnf","type":"Asset","createdAt":"2026-09-20T01:39:08.939Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-20T01:39:08.939Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":2,"revision":1,"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"title":"Best AI SDR for enterprise teams key points","description":"Infographic for the enterprise AI SDR roundup","file":{"url":"//images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/5ptpf9UDcr17VTzMiDLsnf/21938d2451a4cc18941982b05c3c53d1/best-ai-sdr-enterprise-infographic.png","details":{"size":107766,"image":{"width":1080,"height":1080}},"fileName":"best-ai-sdr-enterprise-infographic.png","contentType":"image/png"}}}},"content":[],"nodeType":"embedded-asset-block"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"$4","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What makes Artisan the enterprise pick is the control layer around that autonomy: campaign-level review modes, plain-language escalation rules, per-CRM-field data controls, org-level do-not-contact lists, and a full audit trail. Salesforce and HubSpot sync runs deep, with dynamic list sources, owner mapping, and auto-exclusion of accounts with active deals. The Enterprise plan adds a forward-deployed strategist, dedicated CSM, custom volume, and advanced security and audit logs. Artisan is SOC 2 Type II compliant with GDPR-compliant data handling, with SSO and SAML, plus role-based access using built-in and custom roles.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The results are public: SumUp generates leads at $52 CPL, CookUnity runs 100,000+ emails of targeted outreach, and Chain of Events sourced over $700k of ARR in six months, 20x its investment. None of this replaces the team. Ava does the grunt work so reps can spend their day selling. ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/pricing"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"Pricing","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" scales from self-serve to custom enterprise volume.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Best for:","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" enterprise teams that want an AI employee to own outbound end to end, with autonomy they can dial up or down.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"2. Regie.ai","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Regie.ai comes at the category from sales engagement, and it shows in enterprise credibility: governance, an AI dialer, and a philosophy of AI as rep-augmenting rather than rep-owning. That heritage cuts both ways. Reps still drive the motion, so you scale output per rep rather than scaling pipeline independently of headcount, and it's less autonomous end to end than Artisan.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Best for:","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" enterprises with large existing SDR teams that want AI assistance inside a familiar sales engagement model.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"3. Salesforce Agentforce SDR","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"For organizations standardized on Salesforce, Agentforce SDR has obvious appeal: it's native to the CRM and inherits Salesforce's security posture. Know what you're signing up for, though. Setup is steep, the consumption-based Flex Credits pricing is evolving and hard to forecast, and the product is young. It also works the contacts already in your CRM rather than sourcing net-new pipeline at scale, which is the core job for most enterprise outbound teams. For a deeper look, see our guide to the best AI SDR for enterprise Salesforce teams.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Best for:","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" Salesforce-standardized enterprises prioritizing native CRM residency over net-new sourcing.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"4. Apollo","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Apollo is an excellent database (240M contacts and 30M companies) and a price-accessible all-in-one used by 600,000+ companies. Many enterprises already license it as a data layer. As an AI SDR, Apollo's AI is assistive rather than autonomous: humans still build lists, run sequences, and handle replies. The per-seat model means costs scale with headcount, which is the opposite of what an AI SDR should do.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Best for:","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" teams that want strong data and tooling for human-run outbound at accessible pricing.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"5. Clay","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Clay is the power tool for GTM engineers: best-in-class enrichment orchestration across 200+ data providers, loved by ops teams. What it won't do is send, reply, or book anything on its own. It's infrastructure, and it needs a skilled operator to run, the \"$200K GTM engineer tax.\" Where Clay hands your builders a toolkit, Ava shows up and does the work.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Best for:","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" enterprises with dedicated GTM engineering teams building custom data pipelines.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"6. 11x (Alice and Julian)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"11x is included because enterprise buyers will encounter it: the company has raised about $74M in venture funding, led by a $50M Series B from a16z, claims a 400M+ contact database, and sells through enterprise-style contracts with longer onboarding cycles and no self-serve option, so you commit before you can trial. Its center of gravity is lower mid-market despite that sales motion. Alice handles digital outbound while Julian, an AI phone agent, is positioned mainly on inbound, converting inbound leads over voice, SMS, email, and WhatsApp. Churned customers have cited deliverability issues and CRM-sync complexity, so pressure-test both in your evaluation.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"value":"Best for:","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" lower mid-market teams that want an AI phone agent and are comfortable with opaque contract pricing.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Comparison table","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Platform","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Best for","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"dat